<title>EGYPT: Egypt raises export prices for four cotton grades.</title>
<headline>Egypt raises export prices for four cotton grades.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1996-12-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Egyptian exporters increased by two centilibres (U.S. cents per lb) export prices for four grades of cotton but kept prices for the three remaining grades unchanged, the Alexandria Cotton Exporters Association (Alcotexa) said on Sunday.</p>
<p>The association said prices for Giza 76, Giza 70, Giza 77 and Giza 75 were increased.</p>
<p>The prices in centilibres (valid until 2200 GMT January 4) are:</p>
<p>	     FG/EX    FG+1/4     FG     FG-1/4    G/FG    G+3/8</p>
<p> Giza 76   180.0    174.0    168.0    162.0    156.0    153.0</p>
<p> Giza 70   173.0    167.0    161.0    155.0    149.0    146.0</p>
<p> Giza 77   168.0    162.0    156.0    150.0    144.0    141.0</p>
<p> Giza 75   142.0    136.0    130.0    124.0    118.0    115.0</p>
<p> Giza 85   131.0    125.0    119.0    113.0    107.0    104.0</p>
<p> Giza 83   127.0    121.0    115.0    109.0    103.0    100.0</p>
<p> Giza 80   127.0    121.0    115.0    109.0    103.0    100.0</p>
<p>Note - FG/EX = fully good/excellent, G/FG = good/fully good</p>
<p>-- Cairo newsroom +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
</text>
